october is breast cancer awareness month  and early detection is key hope cancer  care of nevada explains the importance  of self-exams warning signs and the  advances that have been made to fight  breast cancer  [Music]  we are here at hope cancer care of  nevada with the founder and board  certified medical oncologist dr raja  mehdi dr mehdi thank you so much for  talking to us today and as you know  october is breast cancer awareness month  and what are some of the clinical  features and the risk factors for breast  cancer just to put things into  perspective about 275 000 women will be  diagnosed uh  you know on an annual basis with breast  cancer  so about one in eight women will will  see it in their lifetime so it's  extremely important to continue to make  improvements in our outcomes decrease  the mortality and awareness is the key  on the self  exam some of the things that you can  watch for is a lump in the breast or it  could just be a change in the skin of  the breast or a nipple discharge  sometimes  uh women don't feel a lump in the breast  but it's under the arm  so that those are the lymph nodes that  sometimes are swollen without a palpable  mass in the breast that can happen too  just  in the  last 10 years or so  the there's been about 10 percent  reduction in mortality  due to the advancements in screening and  treatments there are many different  treatment options for breast cancer can  you tell us some of those our  momentarium  in fighting  breast cancer has increased to almost a  third of the drugs now  are non-chemotherapy  so  targeted therapies essentially will find  a  target on the surface of the cell  and then they will go attach and either  let our own immune system fight it  or sometimes we can attach the  conventional chemotherapy in a very low  dose  to that target that will deliver it  inside the cell  what age do you suggest that women get  in and start to start taking these  measures getting a mammogram certainly  so the american cancer society at this  time  women starting as early as 40 are  eligible to get mammograms now whatever  the therapy it can be intense when  you're fighting cancer how does hope  cancer center  really try to provide that support to  people during that journey  so first is the the whole personal touch  knowing the patient and the families i  think that's where it starts and then we  have a dedicated team of professionals  to back it up through the treatment if  someone is not doing well  they  have the capability of bringing them in  as a same-day appointment everybody  who's an active treatment  instead of waiting and going to the  hospital they can be brought in and our  team is always ready for them  hope cancer care of nevada has two  locations one here in vegas and one in  pahrump for more information call the  numbers on your screen or visit  hccnevada.com  we'll be right back
 

